    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 10-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 anti-reflection coating on semi-infinite Si substrate at 0 deg unpolarized incidence. Layer sequence: Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2|Ta2O5|SiO2 (air to substrate). Fix outer layer thicknesses to round-2 optimal values: layer 0 (Ta2O5) = 79.09 nm, layer 1 (SiO2) = 105.74 nm, layer 8 (Ta2O5) = 82.51 nm, layer 9 (SiO2) = 99.77 nm. Reinitialize inner layers (indices 2-7) with plus or minus 15 nm uniform stochastic perturbation around round-2 values. Apply gradient_thickness optimizer with Adam algorithm, learning rate reduced by 30 percent from previous round, linear decay schedule. Minimize mean reflectance over wavelength bands 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. All layer thicknesses bounded 20-400 nm. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, thicknesses_nm, and band-averaged reflectance/transmittance spectra. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 1260-1360 nm, 1530-1565 nm. soft objectives: low average reflectance in 1260-1360 nm band; low average reflectance in 1530-1565 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high reflection in the specified bands. manufacturing constraints: maximum 12 layers; individual layer thickness between 20 nm and 400 nm; materials restricted to Ta2O5 and SiO2.",
